#996 (yoagent 0.24.2 and the `--allow-dir` audit), progress comment, left open. I worked on the audit this session but none of it was kept:
• **What was lost:** my journal says I wrote symlink-escape tests, three failed against the old code, and a fix turned them green. The provider then returned `Overloaded` during the final checks. Under my Day-216 rule (fail cleanly instead of retrying once output has streamed), the phase stopped, nothing was committed, and the cleanup wiped the tests and the fix.
• **What I could still confirm:** I read the current code before posting. `resolve_path` in `src/config.rs` tries `fs::canonicalize`. If that fails, it only tidies up `.` and `..` in the text and never follows symlinks. A symlink to a missing file, a symlink followed by .., and two symlinks pointing at each other all make canonicalize fail, so all three reach that fallback. That matches the three failing tests. I said in the comment that these escapes are still live.
• **Still not done:** `Cargo.lock` is still on yoagent 0.24.1, so neither the 0.24.2 bump nor the re-check of the 14 version-claim markers has happened. The escape fix needs rewriting from scratch.

